---
{{ hash_banner() }}
#
# What every authored body in this facility looks like: the material library from
# L0, and which entry each body wears.
#
# WHO READS THIS, because an artifact with no consumer is invented schema. The
# work-piece is the one visible object in the cell that is NOT in any generated
# description — it is spawned into a running world at the moment a scenario or a
# demo needs one, from a model built in code — so it cannot pick its appearance
# up from the scene the way the table, the belts and the pedestals do.
# `cite_bringup.workpiece` builds that model and reads its colour here, which is
# what keeps the spawned box the same orange the model declares instead of a
# third copy of two numbers.
#
# A FACILITY ARTIFACT AND NOT A PER-ZONE ONE. A material is facility-scoped in
# L0 — any type may wear any entry — and emitting a copy per zone would state the
# same colour once per cell, which is the duplication this whole library removes.
#
# FACILITY-SCOPED IS ALSO WHY `bodies` IS KEYED BY TYPE. It answers "what does a
# thing of this kind look like", which is a question about the component library
# and not about where an instance stands. The work-piece has no instances at all
# (ADR-0030) and still has an appearance.
#
# THE LIBRARY AND THE BINDING, NEVER THE JOIN. Each colour appears once, under
# its own name; `bodies` carries names and not colours. Two types wearing one
# material therefore cannot end up two different colours in this file, which is
# the property the library exists for, and a consumer does the join itself.
#
# `ambient` is the colour in shadow, `diffuse` the colour under direct light —
# SDF's own vocabulary, in SDF's own order, red green blue alpha.
appearance:
  materials:
{% if materials %}
{% for material in materials %}
    {{ material.id }}:
      ambient: [{{ material.ambient | map('f') | join(', ') }}]
      diffuse: [{{ material.diffuse | map('f') | join(', ') }}]
{% endfor %}
{% else %}
    {}
{% endif %}
  bodies:
{% if bodies %}
{% for type_id, material_id in bodies %}
    {{ type_id }}: {{ material_id }}
{% endfor %}
{% else %}
    {}
{% endif %}
